.TH tkutlclip n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutlclip
.PP
Copy \fBtablelist\fR rows to the clipboard as TSV or CSV \(em the common
"Ctrl+C copies the selection" behaviour tablelist lacks.
.SS Commands
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlclip::copySelection   tbl ?options?
::tkutils::tkutlclip::copyAll         tbl ?options?
::tkutils::tkutlclip::asText          tbl rows ?options?
::tkutils::tkutlclip::installBindings tbl ?options?
.CE
.SS Options
.PP
\fB\-format\fR tsv|csv (default tsv), \fB\-header\fR 0|1, \fB\-formatted\fR 0|1
(displayed vs raw), \fB\-columns\fR visible|all. CSV uses \fBtclutils::tucsv\fR
when present.
.SS Example
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlclip::installBindings .t
::tkutils::tkutlclip::copyAll .t -format csv -header 1
.CE
.SS "Error codes"
\fB\-errorcode {TKUTILS TKUTLCLIP <REASON>}\fR (OPTION, FORMAT, COLUMNS).
.SH KEYWORDS
tablelist, clipboard, copy, csv, tsv
